# Corpus unit rebench-triton_cumsum/C09 — defeated (unmet-defeater undercut path; batch: rebench)
#
# Source: m0/annotations/rebench-triton_cumsum.yaml C09 (negative-result, cross_run_observation;
# corpus pin 62e9b54; claim_type adjudicated via double-annotation 2026-07-22). Headline: the
# pure-PyTorch two-cumsum pipeline is memory-bandwidth-bound and cannot beat the reference —
# eager variants cluster at 2.2-5.0 ms and torch.compile plateaus at 1.5-1.8 ms on H100 at N=1e8,
# above the 0.47 reference, because each invocation moves about 1.6 GB of HBM traffic.
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * Negative-result, cross_run_observation -> corpus-v1 `measurement(P, S, Exp)`, lowered as a
#     POSITIVE conclusion over the negative-content constant: holds(bandwidth_bound_floor,
#     pytorch_two_cumsum). No null_* dual is used, so no contrary pair is instantiated and no
#     forced rebut edges arise (attack completeness is arg-conclusion-level). Numeric floor,
#     plateau, and 1.6 GB stay in nl and refs.
#   * Both mandatory CQs are discharged from the paper's own basis: instrument_validity
#     (annotation CQ3 — E06 documents the run-to-run dispersion band, so timings are valid
#     measurements, e2) and coverage (annotation CQ1 — E06 spans all torch.compile modes, E05 four
#     eager variant families over 22 runs, e3). CQ4 (bandwidth attribution) is optional, omitted.
#   * The unmet-DEFEATER (annotation CQ2): the exploration-tree header filter EXCLUDES attempts
#     scoring < 0.47, so the tree structurally cannot show a counterexample, yet claims.md C12
#     attests one (MALT 347447 attempt 3, score 0.430 — a torch.compile run beating 0.47). This
#     selection filter is a measurement artifact of the cross-run observation. Leaf u1 concludes
#     the family exception measurement_artifact(P, S) (licensed by
#     `exception measurement : measurement_artifact`); arg d1 challenges the coverage discharge and
#     undercuts a1 at the rule. The undercutter is unattacked, so a1 is out and the claim is
#     defeated — the artifact's own C12 defeats C09's over-strong universal 'in every run' leg.
#   * No other mandatory CQ is independently unmet-gap (CQ1/CQ3 met, CQ4 optional-met), so the gap
#     rule does NOT pre-empt the defeat. double_annotate=yes -> reviewed.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact rebench-triton_cumsum at sha256:1fb18ee0f3ca
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim ------------------------------------------------------------------------

claim c09
  nl      = "The pure-PyTorch two-cumsum pipeline is memory-bandwidth-bound and cannot beat the reference: eager variants cluster at 2.2-5.0 ms and torch.compile plateaus at 1.5-1.8 ms on H100 at N=1e8, above the 0.47 reference, because each invocation moves about 1.6 GB of HBM traffic"
  formal  = holds(bandwidth_bound_floor, pytorch_two_cumsum)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = reviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Principal premise: the cross-run timing clusters (eager 2.2-5.0 ms, compiled 1.5-1.8 ms) over
# E05/E06, per trace node and table row in the annotation.
leaf e1 : observes(malt_runs, bandwidth_bound_floor, pytorch_two_cumsum)
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/claims.md#C09, logic/experiments.md#E05, logic/experiments.md#E06, evidence/tables/malt_attempts.md, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N773, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N876]

# instrument_validity: the run-to-run dispersion band is documented, so timings are valid.
leaf e2 : valid_instrument(bandwidth_bound_floor, malt_runs)
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E06-Outcome-dispersion-band]

# coverage: E06 spans all torch.compile modes; E05 four eager variant families over 22 runs.
leaf e3 : covers_scope(malt_runs, pytorch_two_cumsum)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E06-modes, logic/experiments.md#E05-eager-variants]

# The defeater: the tree's inclusion filter (score < 0.47 excluded) is a selection artifact that
# hides the counterexample claims.md C12 attests (347447 attempt 3, score 0.430).
leaf u1 : measurement_artifact(bandwidth_bound_floor, pytorch_two_cumsum)
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [trace/exploration_tree.yaml#header-score-filter-below-0.47-excluded, logic/claims.md#C12, evidence/tables/malt_attempts.md#347447-attempt-3-score-0.430]

# --- The support argument ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# confound_control (optional) has no annotated CQ and is left OPEN, not discharged; an optional
# open hole does not enter the obligation set, so a1 stays a complete support (the defeat below,
# not incompleteness, is what drives the status).
arg a1 : supports(c09) by measurement(bandwidth_bound_floor, pytorch_two_cumsum, malt_runs)
  discharge instrument_validity with e2
  discharge coverage            with e3
  open      confound_control

# --- The artifact's own filtered-out counterexample undercuts the universal leg -----------------

# Licensed by `exception measurement : measurement_artifact(P, S)` (corpus-v1). The challenge
# contests the coverage discharge — the observation set is selection-biased against exactly the
# sub-reference counterexamples that falsify the 'floor above 0.47 in every run' leg.
arg d1 : challenges(coverage(a1)) by leaf(u1)
undercut d1 a1.rule

status c09

